/-! Data of the bitset certificate for the Tenth binary forest.

The 87 roots are one point of each orbit of the group generated by the six gated Tenth letters
on the singular binary masks: for the 65 type-four orbits a point nearest to Ω under the ten odd
source letters, and the least mask of each of the 22 remaining orbits (short classes and zero).
The 24 doubling steps are words in the six letters together with row operations computing the
binary matrix of each word. All data are discovery outputs; the kernel checks every use. -/

@[expose] public section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster

instance (o : ℕ × ℕ) : Decidable (TenthForestRowValid o) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Decidable (_ ∧ _))

